2. In these Regulations, unless the context otherwise requires —
[Deleted by S 647/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
“counsel” means an advocate and solicitor of the Supreme Court or a foreign lawyer as defined under section 2(1) of the Legal Profession Act 1966;
[S 647/2026 wef 31/12/2021]
“dispute” means a dispute between a casino operator and a patron of the casino as to alleged winnings, alleged losses or the manner in which any casino gambling is conducted;
[S 647/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
“dispute resolution period” has the meaning ascribed to it in regulation 3;
“parties”, in relation to any proceedings for a reconsideration in respect of a dispute, means the casino operator and the patron concerned in the dispute;
[S 647/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
“Patron Dispute Committee” means the committee appointed by the Authority under section 112(4) of the Act to reconsider an inspector’s decision;
“reconsideration” means an appeal to the Authority under section 112(1) of the Act to reconsider an inspector’s decision.
[S 647/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
